    a0 = 9.36032e-11 / 1.13120e-10 m/s^2 (FP0); xi floors 0.02428 / 0.02683 pc (FP7 A4 AQUAL, binding ['M', '2.00']); QUMOND floors 0.0294 / 0.0316 pc
    FP14 F14p: xi is the gravity core's one remaining knob, bounded to [0.0243/0.0268 pc, ~100 pc]
    FP13 H1: L(z = 0) = 2879 kpc, y_th(z = 0) = 0.0 (the yield's switch max(0, 2q) is off while the leaf accelerates); the band-pass's Mpc leg moves the pair's relative force by ~(s/L)^3 = 1.3e-22 at 30 kAU
    FP14 F14d: no scored observable depends on alpha_c beyond O(alpha_c) <= 1.6e-09; the Solar-System alphas vanish as alpha_c -> 0; FP5's y* does not exist on the AQUAL root
    quasi-static: the scalar's signal speed c_s = c sqrt(C_phi/lambda_eff) ~ 1.06 c (lambda_eff = 3 at lambda = 0, c_2 -> oo, C_phi ~ mu_T = 3.36); a 2-Msun pair at 30 kAU orbits at 0.24 km/s: retardation ~ v/c_s = 7.7e-07
